/* bsdgames — shared runtime boundary + per-game adapters for the BSD games
 * set (C loadable). One loadable owns dispatch, data/state/score policy, and
 * the per-game implementations. Per-game .sh stubs run `builtin bsdgames
 * GAME "$@"`. This first slice ships the foundation verbs plus a batch of
 * deterministic, non-interactive computational games (primes, number, morse,
 * caesar, rot13). Full/heavy games (rogue, larn, hack, …) live in the bsdgames
 * PAYLOAD (build-bsdgames-payload.sh), NOT this loadable — see docs/PAYLOAD-MIGRATION.md.
 *
 * See research/bash-os/IMPL-PLANS/bsdgames/01-bsdgames-loadable-and-stubs.md.
 */
